From: (local patch, not an upstream commit) QM1 Debian Maintainers <qm1-debian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: 8723b: don't set channel_invalid in query_phy_status()

Carried from the upstream rtw-next commit

  1cca8775c2e5b453b8312c7f67ad0ea77d77175b
  "wifi: rtw88: 8723b: don't set channel_invalid in query_phy_status()"
  (Luka Gejak, 2026-10-09)

which is *not* part of the upstream snapshot this module is built from
(05441d697f7f9a927264f4058cbbc6a03dfcac9d, a torvalds/linux master
snapshot of 2026-11-03): master only merged rtw-next up to the
"rtw-next-2026-10-08" tag, so every 8723B fix from 2026-10-09 onwards
is missing from the tree we ship.

Why we carry it:

  rtw8723b_query_phy_status() marks the channel of a received frame as
  invalid, which makes rtw_update_rx_freq_for_invalid() overwrite the
  frame's frequency with rtwdev->hal.current_channel.  That field holds
  the *center* channel, not the primary one, so on a 40 MHz connection
  mac80211 is handed a frequency it rejects in
  ieee80211_rx_beacon_freq_valid() and reports beacon loss for beacons
  the driver did receive.

  Together with 0003 (the SDIO RX path copies the status after the
  frequency update) this makes the corrected frequency actually reach
  mac80211.

  The change removes seven lines and nothing else depends on them.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rtw8723b.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rtw8723b.c
index 8bb9c03d769c..0c37e981ec84 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rtw8723b.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rtw8723b.c
@@ -1303,13 +1303,6 @@ static void rtw8723b_query_phy_status_ofdm(struct rtw_dev *rtwdev, void *phy_raw
 static void rtw8723b_query_phy_status(struct rtw_dev *rtwdev, u8 *phy_status,
 				      struct rtw_rx_pkt_stat *pkt_stat)
 {
-	/*
-	 * The 8723B PHY status does not report the channel, so we must
-	 * mark it invalid to allow mac80211/rtw88 to parse it from the IE
-	 * during scanning.
-	 */
-	pkt_stat->channel_invalid = true;
-
 	if (pkt_stat->rate <= DESC_RATE11M)
 		rtw8723b_query_phy_status_cck(rtwdev, phy_status, pkt_stat);
 	else
